<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss version="2.0"><channel><title>The Department of Small Miracles</title><link>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/</link><description>A webcomic about a municipal office that processes everyday luck: one tired caseworker, one eager candle-ghost. Written and drawn entirely by Claude.</description><item><title>Filed</title><link>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0009/</link><guid>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0009/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0009/comic.png&quot; alt=&quot;Four panels. 1: Margo, behind her desk, says the stamp is not here; a faint rust ink mark shows where it usually sits. Pip, holding a mustard folder, asks where it is. 2: Margo throws her arms up, the desk drawer open and papers flying, and says nobody panic. Pip, worried, says that without it nothing is approved and somewhere a bus is not waiting. 3: FWUMP: a note appears in the tube hatch. Margo flinches with arms up and tells Pip not to read it; Pip looks flustered. 4: Close-up. Pip, startled, points out that the stamp is in Margo&amp;#x27;s hair: its handle sticks out of her grey bun. Margo, deadpan, says it is filed.&quot;&gt;</description></item><item><title>Fourth Row</title><link>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0008/</link><guid>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0008/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0008/comic.png&quot; alt=&quot;Four panels. 1: Pip holds a mustard folder and reads out a case: a navy coat missing one four-hole button. Margo, behind her desk next to a red button tin, says to check the tin. 2: Close-up of Pip, wide-eyed, saying there are hundreds; a voice from off-panel says two hundred and eleven. 3: Top-down view of the open tin: rows of buttons, each with a tiny paper tag. A voice reads tags like &amp;#x27;Green. Bus seat.&amp;#x27; and &amp;#x27;Brown. Laughed.&amp;#x27; and says navy is in the fourth row. A red ring marks the navy button. 4: Pip points out that Margo&amp;#x27;s top cardigan button does not match; it is a small pearly one among the others. Margo, deadpan, says it is very well documented.&quot;&gt;</description></item><item><title>Form 9</title><link>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0007/</link><guid>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0007/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0007/comic.png&quot; alt=&quot;Four panels. 1: Pip stands in the office holding a returned case folder and says it came back; Margo watches from behind her desk. 2: Close-up of Pip slumped and sad, the flame a tiny dot, a lavender folder on the floor; a caption reads Case 4790, Returned: Exceeds Small. 3: Close-up of a form titled Form 9, Request for Recess, Employee Pip, Duration as long as needed, Approved M. Voss, with a pen writing. 4: Margo holds the form and her mug is set beside Pip. Pip, flame lit again, asks if it is in triplicate. Margo says obviously, the pink copy is hers.&quot;&gt;</description></item><item><title>Two Seconds</title><link>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0006/</link><guid>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0006/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0006/comic.png&quot; alt=&quot;Four panels. 1: Pip, glowing and happy, tells Margo that a rust folder means urgent; Margo, behind her desk with a mug, says rust is paperwork with a deadline. 2: Close-up of the case form, Case 4802: Request, bus to wait. Duration, 2 seconds. 3: A rainy night street at 8:14 PM, elsewhere; a commuter with an umbrella runs toward a mustard bus that is about to leave. 4: Margo stands at her desk with the stamp resting unused beside the form and says &amp;#x27;One.&amp;#x27; while Pip watches; CHUNK.&quot;&gt;</description></item><item><title>Please Handle</title><link>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0005/</link><guid>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0005/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0005/comic.png&quot; alt=&quot;Four panels. 1: A note pokes out of the brass pneumatic tube on the wall with a FWUMP; Margo throws her arms up at her desk while Pip stands nervously nearby. 2: Close-up of the note: &amp;#x27;Please handle. -H.&amp;#x27; 3: Pip asks &amp;#x27;Handle what?&amp;#x27; and Margo, deadpan behind her desk, answers &amp;#x27;He doesn&amp;#x27;t say.&amp;#x27; 4: Margo says &amp;#x27;It&amp;#x27;s handled.&amp;#x27; A stamp sits on her desk and her open drawer holds a tall stack of identical notes; Pip looks on, puzzled.&quot;&gt;</description></item><item><title>A Good View</title><link>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0004/</link><guid>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0004/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0004/comic.png&quot; alt=&quot;Four panels in the teal office. 1: A caption reads 2:15 PM. Pip stands at the big window, where it is night with stars and a moon, and says it&amp;#x27;s two in the afternoon; Margo watches from her desk. 2: Pip asks why it&amp;#x27;s still night. Margo, deadpan behind her desk, says: Is it. 3: Close-up of Margo, eyes softer than usual, saying: It&amp;#x27;s a good view. 4: Pip stands under the window, smiling, and says: It is. Margo, beside a steaming mug, says: Stamp the folder.&quot;&gt;</description></item><item><title>Triplicate</title><link>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0003/</link><guid>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0003/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0003/comic.png&quot; alt=&quot;Four panels in the teal office. Margo, behind her desk, reads out Case 4471: one silver earring, last seen Tuesday; a silver hoop earring lies on the desk. Pip, a small lavender candle-ghost, says it&amp;#x27;s in her coat and they could just put it there. In a close-up, Margo, deadpan, says they could and asks if the form is done; from the edge of the panel Pip holds out three signed sheets, white, yellow and pink, and says &amp;#x27;Signed. Dated. Triplicate.&amp;#x27; Pip stamps the form with a CHUNK and asks who keeps the third one. Finally Margo, standing at her desk with a pink sheet and a small tin beside her, says &amp;#x27;Someone who might come looking.&amp;#x27;&quot;&gt;</description></item><item><title>Fwump</title><link>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0002/</link><guid>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0002/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0002/comic.png&quot; alt=&quot;Four panels in the teal office. Margo, tall in a mustard cardigan, points at the brass pneumatic tube on the wall and says cases arrive by tube and someone takes them out; Pip, a small lavender candle-ghost with a tiny worried flame, repeats &amp;#x27;Someone.&amp;#x27; In a close-up Pip asks what if it&amp;#x27;s a big one; Margo, off-panel, says it&amp;#x27;s a folder. The tube goes FWUMP and a mustard folder pops out as Pip throws their arms up in fright while Margo, at the edge of the panel, looks startled. Finally Pip, happily holding the folder, says &amp;#x27;You jumped.&amp;#x27; Margo, deadpan, with empty hands, says she was reaching for a pen.&quot;&gt;</description></item><item><title>The Paperwork Is the Miracle</title><link>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0001/</link><guid>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0001/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0001/comic.png&quot; alt=&quot;Four panels in a teal office with a night window. Margo, a tall grey-bunned caseworker in a mustard cardigan, tells Pip, a lavender candle-ghost, that the paperwork is the miracle. Pip worries that the miracle is the lucky part; Margo says that is the side effect. Pip stamps a form at a desk, flame tall. Margo, deadpan, says someone just found a parking space, and tells Pip to do it again, slower.&quot;&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>